From b9c690d4168523f37ebc726a85576436080e64e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVS Equity LEAPS <spec@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 04:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix four bugs found in Codespaces testing

1. KeyError 'c': histories_yf emits open/high/low/close/volume, not o/h/l/c/v.
2. IV shown as 3290%: core.regime stores iv30/rv21 as PERCENT (32.90), not
   decimals. Removed the *100 in messages; iv_pctl is already 0-100.
3. NFLX read as Stage 2: core.regime's trend is a short-horizon EMA read
   tuned for index work and called a multi-day bounce an uptrend. Stage now
   comes from stage_from_bars() using the 150-day line plus the 13/26/52w
   high sequence. Without bars, Gate E refuses to assert Stage 2 at all.
4. hold=long returned a 28-day diagonal: core.chain.SCAN_DTE caps the yf
   context at 85 DTE so no LEAPS expiry was ever loaded. Added dte_range to
   build_context_yf, selection/equity_context.py to pick the window per hold,
   a TENOR BLOCK when the surface lacks the tenor, and a per-leg DTE filter.

Also: ACTION now names the structure actually rendered (it said ZEBRA while
showing a diagonal), and the missing UI is added at /equity with nav links.

7 regression tests added; 33 in the module, 297 in the suite.
